cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DentIndices in your research, please cite it as below, together with the original publication of each index you use (dentindices cite <index>)."
title: "DentIndices: open, tested oral-health epidemiology indices"
abstract: >-
  DentIndices computes the indices used in oral-health surveys, trials and clinics: DMFT/DMFS and
  dmft/dmfs with WHO 2013 coding, SiC, SaC, care and restorative indices, PUFA, BPE and the
  simplified BPE for under-18s, CPITN, the WHO 2013 CPI and loss of attachment, the Plaque and
  Gingival Index, the Plaque Control Record, OHI-S, BEWE, Dean's index and the Community Fluorosis
  Index, the Dental Aesthetic Index, and the CDC/AAP and ACES periodontitis case definitions. Every
  rule is kept in one machine-readable registry with its source, a verification level and a
  documented decision wherever sources disagree; every result returns its components, band,
  guidance, warnings and a step-by-step trace. It ships as a dependency-free Python package and
  command-line tool and as a private in-browser application whose JavaScript engine is tested for
  identical output against the Python package.
